# Plans + team permissions — new features

**Non-negotiable:** every **new product capability** (host dashboard feature, paid module, gated action, new settings surface) must **decide** Plans and Team RBAC in the **same** change — not as a follow-up.

This is the Cursor always-on gate. Full checklist: **`plans-and-permissions`** skill (`.agent/skills/plans-and-permissions/SKILL.md`). Claude Code / OpenCode: invoke that skill before claiming done.

## Mandatory decision (before / during implementation)

Answer both. “Forgot” is not valid.

| Control              | Question                                                       | If **yes**                                                                     | If **no**                                                            |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Plans**            | Should this be limited by subscription tier?                   | Add `PlanFeatureKey`, seed migration, gates, matrix, compare/tier cards        | Note **N/A** in the route guide or workflow doc (why free / ungated) |
| **Team permissions** | Should some team roles be blocked from viewing or mutating it? | Add permission leaf(s), catalog, server allow-list, seeded templates, UI gates | Note **N/A** (owner-only / already covered by an existing leaf)      |

Reference implementation: **Airbnb Channel sync** — plan key `calendarSync` (Pro+) + leaves `pricing.channels:view` / `:edit`.

## Do not ship without

When Plans applies: migration on `pricing_plans.features`, typed keys in UI + edge `planFeatures.ts`, `useFeatureGate` / `requirePropertyFeature`, `docs/architecture/plans-feature-matrix.md`, `planPresentation` / public pricing when host-visible.

Plan tests (Plans applies): update `ui/src/features/dashboard/plans/lib/planTierGolden.ts` (tier values, `GOLDEN_MINIMUM_TIER`), `planTierExpectations.ts` (literal card bullets, Compare rows, review-dialog unlock lists) and the `GATE_COVERAGE` map in `planGateCoverage.test.ts`; then run `bun run check:plan-catalog` against a fresh local DB. These fail when a key, tier, card bullet, Compare row or gate is added or changed without a decision.

When Team RBAC applies: UI `propertyTeamConstants` (and parking/org mirrors if needed) + edge `propertyTeamPermissions` (etc.) **in sync**, `propertyPermissionCatalog` (plan pills derive from `PLAN_FEATURE_PERMISSION_COVERAGE` in `plans/lib/planFeaturePermissions.ts` — map every new `PlanFeatureKey` to leaves or an explicit N/A there; a unit test enforces it), a backfill migration when a leaf is split from an existing one (never read-time expansion for live leaves), seeded templates, `resolveScoped*Access` on writes, route-guide permission table.

